WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.089
Agents ask you things.

2
00:00:10.089 --> 00:00:13.659
Here is how you answer, without leaving the keyboard.

3
00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:26.860
Ask for a small feature, and tell the leader to check with you first.

4
00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:49.368
The leader asks, with its choices as options.

5
00:00:49.368 --> 00:00:54.362
A digit answers with one of them; slash would let you write your own.

6
00:01:03.513 --> 00:01:09.444
A worker builds it, and its change waits for you, before anything ran.

7
00:01:24.014 --> 00:01:25.501
Read the change.

8
00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:30.147
C puts a note on the line at hand; enter keeps it.

9
00:01:30.147 --> 00:01:36.465
N sends every note back to the worker, each under its file and line.

10
00:01:48.815 --> 00:01:53.587
Now the worker wants to run a command that is not a test, so it asks you.

11
00:01:53.587 --> 00:01:58.948
A allows this command from now on, for the whole project; e would allow everything

12
00:01:58.948 --> 00:02:00.255
until its turn ends.

13
00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:05.746
If the item changed under you, imece asks you to read it first, and you press again.

14
00:02:16.817 --> 00:02:22.028
The worker ran the command on a scratch file, and proposed its change again.

15
00:02:31.719 --> 00:02:32.794
A approves.

16
00:02:32.794 --> 00:02:36.410
Lonca runs the tests, then merges it.

17
00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:48.751
Every answer is a key: a, r, e, A, a digit, or a note.

18
00:02:49.553 --> 00:02:53.564
The cheat sheet on the site has every key on one page.

